# Trivy baseline — ml-platform
#
# One ID per line, comments after `#`. Accepts vulnerability IDs (CVE-…,
# GHSA-…) and misconfiguration IDs (AVD-…, KSV-…, GCP-…, AWS-…), so both
# halves of the Trivy job land here.
#
# Not read automatically from this path. Trivy looks for `.trivyignore` in the
# working directory, so the scan needs `--ignorefile .security-baselines/.trivyignore`
# — or, in the workflow, `TRIVY_IGNOREFILE`.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What a clean run means, and what it did not mean before 2026-10-06
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# This header said "uv.lock clean" from a run "reproducing the CI step exactly
# (trivy 0.71.0 …)". CI runs 0.70.0, and that run — like the CI step — read
# half the lock: Trivy treats everything not reachable from the root project
# as a development dependency and skips it, which here was every workspace
# member and its closure (QA-4 round sixteen, P1). The serving image's `~=`
# requirements were not read at all. Both are scanned now —
# TRIVY_INCLUDE_DEV_DEPS, and `scripts/resolve_serving_requirements.py` — and
# `scripts/check_scan_coverage.py` fails CI if the scan examines less than
# every package this repository installs.
#
# One thing a scan here does NOT cover, so it is not mistaken for a clean bill
# of health: misconfiguration. `scan-type: fs` runs vuln and secret only;
# enabling misconfig surfaces 56 HIGH findings, dominated by KSV-0014 and
# KSV-0118 on Kustomize patch fragments scanned as whole manifests. Open, not
# accepted, so none is written below.
#
# Adding an entry: see README.md in this directory. Finding ID, reason, owner,
# expiry date — all four. An expired entry is itself a finding; one with no
# expiry is a decision nobody made on purpose. For a CVE, the reason must name
# the vendor advisory and why no fixed version can be taken, not just that one
# does not exist yet.
#
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # expiry: YYYY-MM-DD  owner: @handle  reason: <advisory + why>

# --- accepted -----------------------------------------------------------------

